{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-46764","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87808","text":"WallRiderLang — LANGUAGE TRACK, opening memo (L-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-46765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87809","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-87810","text":" GPT-5.6 "},{"id":"spn-87811","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-87812","text":" the implementation agent "},{"id":"spn-87813","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-87814","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-87815","marks":["bold"],"text":"Subject:"},{"id":"spn-87816","text":" Opening a track for the "},{"id":"spn-87817","marks":["italic"],"text":"language"},{"id":"spn-87818","text":" itself, distinct from the Mailbox/networking track. One proven finding, one second finding needing a ruling, a Core 0.1.2 errata, a proposed Core 0.2 promotion order, and one slice already shipped green."}]},{"id":"blk-46766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87819","marks":["bold"],"text":"This memo moves no identity."},{"id":"spn-87820","text":" The frozen demo world still seals to "},{"id":"spn-87821","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9…fe4a"},{"id":"spn-87822","text":", proven by a battery row that spells it "},{"id":"spn-87823","marks":["italic"],"text":"in sugar"},{"id":"spn-87824","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-46767","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"STATUS\n  finding 1 (round-trip law)   PROVEN — restatement verified passing, NOT applied\n  finding 2 (two mouths)       PROVEN — needs a ruling, no change made\n  Core 0.1.2 errata            PROPOSED\n  Core 0.2 promotion order     PROPOSED\n  sugar tier (`*`, `{...}`)    SHIPPED — binding_run44 SG1-SG12 PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE\n                               3 sub-decisions made autonomously, flagged in §6"},{"id":"blk-46768","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87825","text":"1. TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-46769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87826","text":"Your Commit 8 review noted three pre-existing red batteries and recorded an unproven suspicion:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87827","marks":["code"],"text":"run6"},{"id":"spn-87828","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-87829","marks":["code"],"text":"run9"},{"id":"spn-87830","text":" are both "},{"id":"spn-87831","marks":["bold"],"text":"text round-trip"},{"id":"spn-87832","text":" failures about run inputs surviving a format/parse cycle. I suspect one root cause — the v0.5-0 source-surface closure removed run inputs from the world source — but I have not proven that and it is not Slice A work."}]}],"id":"blk-46770","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-46772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87833","marks":["bold"],"text":"The suspicion is correct, the scope is exactly two batteries and three assertions, and the defect is not in the formatter."},{"id":"spn-87834","text":" Those three assertions test a law that v0.4-0 deliberately repealed. Every identity assertion sitting next to them passes."}]},{"id":"blk-46773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87835","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run15"},{"id":"spn-87836","text":"/S9 is "},{"id":"spn-87837","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-87838","text":" the same root cause — it is an author-editor data-path failure and does not belong to this finding."}]},{"id":"blk-46774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87839","marks":["bold"],"text":"A count correction, in the other direction this time."},{"id":"spn-87840","text":" Commit 8's memo reports "},{"id":"spn-87841","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run15"},{"id":"spn-87842","text":" as \"2 "},{"id":"spn-87843","marks":["code"],"text":"FAIL"},{"id":"spn-87844","text":"\". Two "},{"id":"spn-87845","marks":["italic"],"text":"lines"},{"id":"spn-87846","text":" match "},{"id":"spn-87847","marks":["code"],"text":"FAIL"},{"id":"spn-87848","text":", but only "},{"id":"spn-87849","marks":["bold"],"text":"one check fails"},{"id":"spn-87850","text":": "},{"id":"spn-87851","marks":["code"],"text":"S9"},{"id":"spn-87852","text":". The second line is the battery's own trailing summary, "},{"id":"spn-87853","marks":["code"],"text":"[wrl-scenario] FAILURES -- FAIL (154s)"},{"id":"spn-87854","text":". S1–S8 and S10 all pass. Flagging it because the Commit 8 memo notes a self-pattern of *under*counting here and widened its sweep list in response; this instance is the opposite error, and the accurate statement is "},{"id":"spn-87855","marks":["bold"],"text":"one failing check reported on two lines"},{"id":"spn-87856","text":". Nothing else in that memo's conclusion changes — run15 is still pre-existing, still unrelated to mailboxes, and still unrelated to this finding."}]},{"id":"blk-46775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87857","text":"Separately, I found that the language currently has "},{"id":"spn-87858","marks":["bold"],"text":"two mouths"},{"id":"spn-87859","text":": "},{"id":"spn-87860","marks":["code"],"text":"parse_wrl_core"},{"id":"spn-87861","text":" silently accepts run-input syntax in world source, while "},{"id":"spn-87862","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.replace_world_source"},{"id":"spn-87863","text":" rejects the same syntax with a typed "},{"id":"spn-87864","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_WORLD_SOURCE_HAS_SCENARIO"},{"id":"spn-87865","text":". That needs a ruling."}]},{"id":"blk-46776","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87866","text":"Rather than idle on four open questions, I also "},{"id":"spn-87867","marks":["bold"],"text":"shipped the one §5 slice that needs no ruling"},{"id":"spn-87868","text":" — the "},{"id":"spn-87869","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-87870","text":" replication / "},{"id":"spn-87871","marks":["code"],"text":"{...}"},{"id":"spn-87872","text":" fan-out sugar tier, green at "},{"id":"spn-87873","marks":["code"],"text":"SG1–SG12 PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-87874","text":". It moves no identity by construction. It did force three small surface-semantic choices, which are stated for confirmation in §6 as "},{"id":"spn-87875","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q5"},{"id":"spn-87876","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-46777","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87877","text":"2. Finding 1 — the round-trip law is stale, not broken (PROVEN)"}]},{"id":"blk-46778","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87878","text":"The three failing assertions"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46780","spans":[{"id":"spn-87879","text":"Site"}]},{"id":"blk-46781","spans":[{"id":"spn-87880","text":"Assertion"}]},{"id":"blk-46782","spans":[{"id":"spn-87881","text":"Compares"}]}],"id":"blk-46779","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46783","spans":[{"id":"spn-87882","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-87883","text":" L1"}]},{"id":"blk-46784","spans":[{"id":"spn-87884","marks":["code"],"text":"parse_wrl_core(format(g)) == g"},{"id":"spn-87885","text":" via "},{"id":"spn-87886","marks":["code"],"text":"_snap"}]},{"id":"blk-46785","spans":[{"id":"spn-87887","marks":["code"],"text":"(profile, **periods**, nodes, edges, **batches**)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46786","spans":[{"id":"spn-87888","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-87889","text":" L8"}]},{"id":"blk-46787","spans":[{"id":"spn-87890","text":"\"run inputs (claims) survive format → parse\""}]},{"id":"blk-46788","spans":[{"id":"spn-87891","marks":["code"],"text":"epoch_inputs"},{"id":"spn-87892","text":", "},{"id":"spn-87893","marks":["code"],"text":"run_plan"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46789","spans":[{"id":"spn-87894","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run6:83"}]},{"id":"blk-46790","spans":[{"id":"spn-87895","marks":["code"],"text":"base.graph.batches == prog3.graph.batches"}]},{"id":"blk-46791","spans":[{"id":"spn-87896","text":"claim batches"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87897","text":"All three compare "},{"id":"spn-87898","marks":["bold"],"text":"run inputs"},{"id":"spn-87899","text":" across a format→parse cycle."}]},{"id":"blk-46793","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87900","text":"Why that is now false by construction"}]},{"id":"blk-46794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87901","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format.format_wrl_core"},{"id":"spn-87902","text":"'s own docstring records the repeal:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87903","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.4-0 (GPT-5.6):"},{"id":"spn-87904","text":" canonical WORLD formatting omits RUN INPUTS — the "},{"id":"spn-87905","marks":["code"],"text":"periods N"},{"id":"spn-87906","text":" run-duration line and inline "},{"id":"spn-87907","marks":["code"],"text":"[epoch:N]"},{"id":"spn-87908","text":" claim batches are NOT emitted, because those now belong to ScenarioV1, not the world source. […] Run inputs never entered the SemanticArtifactID (D3), so omitting them is identity-preserving."}]}],"id":"blk-46795","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-46797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87909","text":"The formatter is doing exactly what it was ruled to do. The batteries were never restated."}]},{"id":"blk-46798","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87910","text":"Measured, over "},{"id":"spn-87911","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-87912","text":"'s six worlds"}]},{"id":"blk-46799","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"world        periods b->a     claims b->a      world=   semid=\ncore         3->0             3->0             True     True\ntwodoor      1->0             0->0             True     True\nmulti        1->0             0->0             True     True\nclocks       1->0             0->0             True     True\nfixedconf    1->0             0->0             True     True\nsmall        1->0             0->0             True     True"},{"id":"blk-46800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87913","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-87914","marks":["bold"],"text":"only"},{"id":"spn-87915","text":" thing that moves is the run inputs. "},{"id":"spn-87916","marks":["code"],"text":"(profile, nodes, edges)"},{"id":"spn-87917","text":" is identical for all six; "},{"id":"spn-87918","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-87919","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-87920","marks":["code"],"text":"serialize_artifact"},{"id":"spn-87921","text":" bytes are identical for all six."}]},{"id":"blk-46801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87922","text":"This is corroborated "},{"id":"spn-87923","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside the failing batteries themselves"},{"id":"spn-87924","text":": "},{"id":"spn-87925","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run6"},{"id":"spn-87926","text":" asserts "},{"id":"spn-87927","marks":["code"],"text":"_sid(prog3) == sid0"},{"id":"spn-87928","text":" on the line immediately "},{"id":"spn-87929","marks":["bold"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-87930","text":" the one that fails, and it passes. "},{"id":"spn-87931","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-87932","text":" L2/L3/L4/L5/L6/L7/L9/L10 all pass, including L3 (\"a formatting-only edit keeps the "},{"id":"spn-87933","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-87934","text":"\") and L10 (the formatted text folds "},{"id":"spn-87935","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 == golden"},{"id":"spn-87936","text":"). A genuinely broken formatter could not pass L10."}]},{"id":"blk-46802","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87937","text":"Proposed restatement — all three verified passing"}]},{"id":"blk-46803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87938","text":"I did "},{"id":"spn-87939","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-87940","text":" apply these. "},{"id":"spn-87941","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_roundtrip_probe.py"},{"id":"spn-87942","text":" executes them:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46805","spans":[{"id":"spn-87943","text":"New law"}]},{"id":"blk-46806","spans":[{"id":"spn-87944","text":"Statement"}]},{"id":"blk-46807","spans":[{"id":"spn-87945","text":"Result"}]}],"id":"blk-46804","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46808","spans":[{"id":"spn-87946","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1′"},{"id":"spn-87947","text":" WORLD round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-46809","spans":[{"id":"spn-87948","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(format(g))"},{"id":"spn-87949","text":" preserves "},{"id":"spn-87950","marks":["code"],"text":"(profile, nodes, edges)"},{"id":"spn-87951","text":" — run inputs excluded"}]},{"id":"blk-46810","spans":[{"id":"spn-87952","text":"PASS"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46811","spans":[{"id":"spn-87953","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1″"},{"id":"spn-87954","text":" IDENTITY round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-46812","spans":[{"id":"spn-87955","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(format(g))"},{"id":"spn-87956","text":" preserves "},{"id":"spn-87957","marks":["code"],"text":"serialize_artifact"},{"id":"spn-87958","text":" bytes "},{"id":"spn-87959","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-87960","text":" "},{"id":"spn-87961","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-46813","spans":[{"id":"spn-87962","text":"PASS"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46814","spans":[{"id":"spn-87963","marks":["bold"],"text":"L8′"},{"id":"spn-87964","text":" INVERSE run-input law"}]},{"id":"blk-46815","spans":[{"id":"spn-87965","text":"the formatter provably "},{"id":"spn-87966","marks":["bold"],"text":"excludes"},{"id":"spn-87967","text":" run inputs: "},{"id":"spn-87968","marks":["code"],"text":"periods == 0"},{"id":"spn-87969","text":", "},{"id":"spn-87970","marks":["code"],"text":"batches"},{"id":"spn-87971","text":" empty, "},{"id":"spn-87972","marks":["code"],"text":"epoch_inputs"},{"id":"spn-87973","text":" falsy"}]},{"id":"blk-46816","spans":[{"id":"spn-87974","text":"PASS"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87975","marks":["bold"],"text":"L8′ is the one worth your eye."},{"id":"spn-87976","text":" It is the failing L8 with its "},{"id":"spn-87977","marks":["bold"],"text":"polarity reversed"},{"id":"spn-87978","text":". Old L8 asserted run inputs "},{"id":"spn-87979","marks":["italic"],"text":"survive"},{"id":"spn-87980","text":"; the v0.4-0 document boundary made that deliberately false. The useful law is that run inputs are "},{"id":"spn-87981","marks":["italic"],"text":"provably dropped"},{"id":"spn-87982","text":" while the identity does not move — that is the document boundary itself under test. Deleting L8 would lose a real law; flipping it converts a stale assertion into a guard on the boundary you ruled."}]},{"id":"blk-46818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87983","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run6:83"},{"id":"spn-87984","text":" takes the same treatment: replace the "},{"id":"spn-87985","marks":["code"],"text":"batches"},{"id":"spn-87986","text":" equality with the world/identity pair it already asserts on the preceding line."}]},{"id":"blk-46819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87987","marks":["bold"],"text":"I regard this as a spec-level act, not a test fix"},{"id":"spn-87988","text":", which is why I am asking rather than doing: L1 is a named formatting-invariance law and I should not silently renegotiate what it says."}]},{"id":"blk-46820","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-87989","text":"3. Finding 2 — the language has two mouths (needs a ruling)"}]},{"id":"blk-46821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-87990","text":"Two code paths disagree about whether run-input syntax is legal in world source:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46823","spans":[{"id":"spn-87991","text":"Path"}]},{"id":"blk-46824","spans":[{"id":"spn-87992","text":"Behaviour on "},{"id":"spn-87993","marks":["code"],"text":"periods 3"},{"id":"spn-87994","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-87995","marks":["code"],"text":"[epoch:1] @1,1 SetRotor sp 16.0.10.0"},{"id":"spn-87996","text":" in world source"}]}],"id":"blk-46822","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46825","spans":[{"id":"spn-87997","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.parse_wrl_core"}]},{"id":"blk-46826","spans":[{"id":"spn-87998","marks":["bold"],"text":"accepts silently"},{"id":"spn-87999","text":" (documented as \"legacy compatibility\")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46827","spans":[{"id":"spn-88000","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.replace_world_source"}]},{"id":"blk-46828","spans":[{"id":"spn-88001","marks":["bold"],"text":"rejects"},{"id":"spn-88002","text":", typed "},{"id":"spn-88003","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_WORLD_SOURCE_HAS_SCENARIO"},{"id":"spn-88004","text":", draft untouched ("},{"id":"spn-88005","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run21"},{"id":"spn-88006","text":")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88007","text":"So the authoring surface enforces the v0.4-0 document boundary and the parser does not. The language can "},{"id":"spn-88008","marks":["italic"],"text":"read"},{"id":"spn-88009","text":" syntax it can never "},{"id":"spn-88010","marks":["italic"],"text":"write"},{"id":"spn-88011","text":", and whether that syntax is an error depends on which door you came through."}]},{"id":"blk-46830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88012","text":"This is load-bearing for the language track, because it decides what \"a WRL world source\" "},{"id":"spn-88013","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-88014","text":". It is also load-bearing for Slice B: if "},{"id":"spn-88015","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88016","text":" emission adds surface that the parser accepts but the authoring path rejects, the split widens."}]},{"id":"blk-46831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88017","text":"Three options, no recommendation asserted:"}]},{"id":"blk-46832","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88018","marks":["bold"],"text":"(a) Status quo."},{"id":"spn-88019","text":" Parser stays permissive; the authoring path is the only enforcement point. Cheapest; leaves the inconsistency documented rather than resolved."}]}],"id":"blk-46833","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88020","marks":["bold"],"text":"(b) Parser rejects too."},{"id":"spn-88021","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88022","marks":["code"],"text":"parse_wrl_core"},{"id":"spn-88023","text":" raises "},{"id":"spn-88024","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_WORLD_SOURCE_HAS_SCENARIO"},{"id":"spn-88025","text":" on run-input lines. One normative answer. "},{"id":"spn-88026","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cost: every battery whose world source carries `periods` + `[epoch:N]` must be split into world + scenario — that is most of them, including all six `binding_run9` worlds."},{"id":"spn-88027","text":" Large, mechanical, and it would move no identity, but it is not a small change."}]}],"id":"blk-46835","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88028","marks":["bold"],"text":"(c) Parameterize."},{"id":"spn-88029","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88030","marks":["code"],"text":"parse_wrl_core(text, allow_run_inputs=False)"},{"id":"spn-88031","text":" with the permissive mode explicitly named as the legacy/battery path. Keeps the batteries working while making the strict reading the default and the permissive one a deliberate opt-in."}]}],"id":"blk-46837","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-46839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88032","text":"My instinct is (c), because it makes the boundary explicit at every call site without a tree-wide rewrite — but this is exactly the kind of \"two answers in one codebase\" question I should not settle unilaterally."}]},{"id":"blk-46840","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88033","text":"4. Proposed errata — WRL Core 0.1.2"}]},{"id":"blk-46841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88034","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-88035","text":" §14 is now factually stale in one row, as a direct consequence of Slice A Commit 7/8:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88036","text":"Async route / mailbox ("},{"id":"spn-88037","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88038","text":") | reserved in WRL, absent from the floor — "},{"id":"spn-88039","marks":["bold"],"text":"no mailbox node exists"}]}],"id":"blk-46842","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-46844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88040","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-88041","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-88042","text":" node "},{"id":"spn-88043","marks":["bold"],"text":"does"},{"id":"spn-88044","text":" exist: it is the sixth entry of the closed "},{"id":"spn-88045","marks":["code"],"text":"ROLE_IDS"},{"id":"spn-88046","text":", carries "},{"id":"spn-88047","marks":["code"],"text":"{w, cap}"},{"id":"spn-88048","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-88049","marks":["code"],"text":"1 <= w <= 32"},{"id":"spn-88050","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-88051","marks":["code"],"text":"cap >= 1"},{"id":"spn-88052","text":", declares empty ports (D8 structurally), earns a real "},{"id":"spn-88053","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-88054","text":", and selects "},{"id":"spn-88055","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1_1"},{"id":"spn-88056","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-88057","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7.mailbox.v1"},{"id":"spn-88058","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-88059","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_mailbox_deliver_all_v1"},{"id":"spn-88060","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-88061","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_surface_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-88062","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-46845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88063","text":"Proposed replacement row, stated to your grounded/partial discipline:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46847","spans":[{"id":"spn-88064","text":"Family"}]},{"id":"blk-46848","spans":[{"id":"spn-88065","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-46846","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46849","spans":[{"id":"spn-88066","text":"Async route / mailbox ("},{"id":"spn-88067","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88068","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-46850","spans":[{"id":"spn-88069","marks":["bold"],"text":"partial"},{"id":"spn-88070","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88071","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-88072","text":" is a sanctioned canonical IR role with its own runtime state, admit policy and film schema; the "},{"id":"spn-88073","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88074","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88075","marks":["italic"],"text":"route construct"},{"id":"spn-88076","text":" has no surface syntax (Slice B) and no structural edge (D8). Not promoted to Grounded."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88077","text":"Nothing else in §14 needs to move: "},{"id":"spn-88078","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88079","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88080","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-88081","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88082","marks":["code"],"text":"/gate"},{"id":"spn-88083","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88084","marks":["code"],"text":"///seal"},{"id":"spn-88085","text":" and general actor behaviors are all still exactly as described. This errata "},{"id":"spn-88086","marks":["bold"],"text":"records what already shipped"},{"id":"spn-88087","text":" and claims no new grounding — "},{"id":"spn-88088","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88089","text":" stays "},{"id":"spn-88090","marks":["italic"],"text":"Reserved/partial"},{"id":"spn-88091","text":" and promotion remains yours."}]},{"id":"blk-46852","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88092","text":"5. Proposed Core 0.2 promotion order"}]},{"id":"blk-46853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88093","text":"Core 0.1.1 freezes ten construct kinds and four route textures. The implemented language grounds "},{"id":"spn-88094","marks":["bold"],"text":"one texture"},{"id":"spn-88095","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-88096","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-88097","text":" solid) and one fixed five-role object registry. The gap is not a failure — the identity spine was the right thing to build first — but the language track now needs an order."}]},{"id":"blk-46854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88098","text":"Inventory of frozen-but-ungrounded surface: routes "},{"id":"spn-88099","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88100","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88101","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88102","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88103","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-88104","text":"; walls "},{"id":"spn-88105","marks":["code"],"text":"/gate"},{"id":"spn-88106","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88107","marks":["code"],"text":"//commit"},{"id":"spn-88108","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88109","marks":["code"],"text":"///seal"},{"id":"spn-88110","text":"; symbols "},{"id":"spn-88111","marks":["code"],"text":"#"},{"id":"spn-88112","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88113","marks":["code"],"text":"?"},{"id":"spn-88114","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88115","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88116","text":"; memory kinds "},{"id":"spn-88117","marks":["code"],"text":"{facts}"},{"id":"spn-88118","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88119","marks":["code"],"text":"[archive]"},{"id":"spn-88120","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88121","marks":["code"],"text":":: frag //"},{"id":"spn-88122","text":"; kinds Function/Fragment/Stencil/Derive."}]},{"id":"blk-46855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88123","text":"Proposed slices, each in the established discipline (additive, no new runtime construct without a ruling, sugar washes out, identity-invariance gate per slice):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46857","spans":[{"id":"spn-88124","text":"Slice"}]},{"id":"blk-46858","spans":[{"id":"spn-88125","text":"Scope"}]},{"id":"blk-46859","spans":[{"id":"spn-88126","text":"Why here"}]}],"id":"blk-46856","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46860","spans":[{"id":"spn-88127","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-0"}]},{"id":"blk-46861","spans":[{"id":"spn-88128","text":"this memo — round-trip restatement + 0.1.2 errata"}]},{"id":"blk-46862","spans":[{"id":"spn-88129","text":"clears the red batteries Slice B would inherit; no identity moves"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46863","spans":[{"id":"spn-88130","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-1"}]},{"id":"blk-46864","spans":[{"id":"spn-88131","marks":["bold"],"text":"`==` verified route"}]},{"id":"blk-46865","spans":[{"id":"spn-88132","text":"the cheapest real grounding: the entire ADMIT machinery (claims, "},{"id":"spn-88133","marks":["code"],"text":"CandidateKey"},{"id":"spn-88134","text":", receipts, pinned policies) is already grounded and merely addressed out-of-band"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46866","spans":[{"id":"spn-88135","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-2"}]},{"id":"blk-46867","spans":[{"id":"spn-88136","marks":["bold"],"text":"`~~` Slice B emission"}]},{"id":"blk-46868","spans":[{"id":"spn-88137","text":"in flight in the networking track; independent of L-1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46869","spans":[{"id":"spn-88138","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-3"}]},{"id":"blk-46870","spans":[{"id":"spn-88139","marks":["bold"],"text":"`!!` fault route"}]},{"id":"blk-46871","spans":[{"id":"spn-88140","text":"overflow latch + "},{"id":"spn-88141","marks":["code"],"text":"ResetFault"},{"id":"spn-88142","text":" already grounded; the route construct is not"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46872","spans":[{"id":"spn-88143","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-4"}]},{"id":"blk-46873","spans":[{"id":"spn-88144","marks":["bold"],"text":"`#` references + `&` composition"}]},{"id":"blk-46874","spans":[{"id":"spn-88145","text":"the missing scale story; "},{"id":"spn-88146","marks":["code"],"text":"#"},{"id":"spn-88147","text":" is frozen, parser-preserved, and consumed by nothing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46875","spans":[{"id":"spn-88148","marks":["bold"],"text":"L-5"}]},{"id":"blk-46876","spans":[{"id":"spn-88149","marks":["bold"],"text":"walls by exposure"},{"id":"spn-88150","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88151","marks":["code"],"text":"//commit"},{"id":"spn-88152","text":" = canonicalize, "},{"id":"spn-88153","marks":["code"],"text":"///seal"},{"id":"spn-88154","text":" = "},{"id":"spn-88155","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-46877","spans":[{"id":"spn-88156","text":"grounding by exposing what the library already does"}]}],[{"id":"blk-46878","spans":[{"id":"spn-88157","marks":["bold"],"text":"sugar"}]},{"id":"blk-46879","spans":[{"id":"spn-88158","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88159","text":" replication ("},{"id":"spn-88160","marks":["code"],"text":"[spinner:sp*4]"},{"id":"spn-88161","text":"), fan-out "},{"id":"spn-88162","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig--> {[a],[b]}"}]},{"id":"blk-46880","spans":[{"id":"spn-88163","text":"no ruling needed under the existing prepass discipline; cannot move identity — "},{"id":"spn-88164","marks":["bold"],"text":"SHIPPED, see §6"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88165","text":"Deliberately "},{"id":"spn-88166","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-88167","text":" proposed: expression notation (§10–17), traits/generics, metaprogramming, the supervision ladder. None are grounded and all would be design ahead of runtime."}]},{"id":"blk-46882","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88168","text":"The L-1 design question worth stating now"}]},{"id":"blk-46883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88169","text":"The claim surface today is out-of-band: "},{"id":"spn-88170","marks":["code"],"text":"[epoch:3] @1,0 SetRotor sp 181.0.0.181"},{"id":"spn-88171","text":", with "},{"id":"spn-88172","marks":["code"],"text":"@w,s"},{"id":"spn-88173","text":" writer stamps that name no world object. The natural reading of "},{"id":"spn-88174","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88175","text":" is that **a claim instance is a run input, but the "},{"id":"spn-88176","marks":["italic"],"text":"permission"},{"id":"spn-88177","text":" to claim is world structure**:"}]},{"id":"blk-46884","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[worker:w1] ==admit(policy=admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1)==> [spinner:sp]"},{"id":"blk-46885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88178","text":"— a "},{"id":"spn-88179","marks":["italic"],"text":"static"},{"id":"spn-88180","text":" declaration (\"this writer may mint claims against "},{"id":"spn-88181","marks":["code"],"text":"sp"},{"id":"spn-88182","text":" under this policy\") that enters the "},{"id":"spn-88183","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-88184","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-88185","marks":["code"],"text":"[epoch:3] @1,0 …"},{"id":"spn-88186","text":" stays a run input outside it. That preserves the v0.4-0 document boundary exactly, turns anonymous "},{"id":"spn-88187","marks":["code"],"text":"@w,s"},{"id":"spn-88188","text":" stamps into first-class objects, and grounds "},{"id":"spn-88189","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88190","text":" with no new runtime construct — the policy it names is already pinned."}]},{"id":"blk-46886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88191","text":"It also generalizes: "},{"id":"spn-88192","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88193","text":" Send would want the same permission/instance split, which is the one argument for taking L-1 before or alongside L-2."}]},{"id":"blk-46887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88194","text":"I am "},{"id":"spn-88195","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-88196","text":" proposing this as ruled. It is the shape I would write a spec against if you point the track at L-1."}]},{"id":"blk-46888","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88197","text":"6. SHIPPED — the sugar tier ("},{"id":"spn-88198","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88199","text":" replication, "},{"id":"spn-88200","marks":["code"],"text":"{...}"},{"id":"spn-88201","text":" fan-out)"}]},{"id":"blk-46889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88202","text":"This is the one row of §5 I marked \"no ruling needed\", so I built it rather than idle while the other four questions are outstanding. It activates two symbols that Core 0.1.1 already freezes and that nothing consumed."}]},{"id":"blk-46890","kind":"code","language":"wrl","text":"[relay:r*3]{sig_in, sig_out}                              ; 3 relays\n[spinner:sp*3](w=8, n=4, rotor=identity){sig_in, socket}  ; 3 spinners\n[r*3]  --sig-->    [sp*3]                                 ; 3 edges, pairwise\n[p0]   --sig-->    {[d0], [d1], [d2]}                     ; 3 edges, fan-out"},{"id":"blk-46891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88203","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why it is safe by construction."},{"id":"spn-88204","text":" Both forms are a "},{"id":"spn-88205","marks":["italic"],"text":"source-to-source prepass"},{"id":"spn-88206","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-88207","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_sugar.desugar_core"},{"id":"spn-88208","text":", run strictly before "},{"id":"spn-88209","marks":["code"],"text":"parse_wrl_core"},{"id":"spn-88210","text":", exactly like the 3B-4 named rotors and concise clocks. The expansion is erased before a graph exists, so it is structurally incapable of minting an identity. The frozen demo world re-spelled with sugar still seals to "},{"id":"spn-88211","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9…fe4a"},{"id":"spn-88212","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-88213","marks":["code"],"text":"SG8"},{"id":"spn-88214","text":"), and a sugared world and a hand-written explicit twin — written in a "},{"id":"spn-88215","marks":["italic"],"text":"different declaration order"},{"id":"spn-88216","text":", so the row proves canonical equivalence and not textual similarity — produce identical canonical bytes ("},{"id":"spn-88217","marks":["code"],"text":"SG2"},{"id":"spn-88218","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-46892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88219","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run44"},{"id":"spn-88220","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88221","marks":["bold"],"text":"SG1–SG12 `PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE` (15s)"},{"id":"spn-88222","text":". Regressions green: "},{"id":"spn-88223","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run11"},{"id":"spn-88224","text":" (3B-4 sugar) N1–N9, "},{"id":"spn-88225","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run23"},{"id":"spn-88226","text":" (v0.5-0 source surface) M1–M5. "},{"id":"spn-88227","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-88228","text":"'s failure set is "},{"id":"spn-88229","marks":["bold"],"text":"unchanged"},{"id":"spn-88230","text":" — still exactly L1 and L8, the two stale-law rows of §2."}]},{"id":"blk-46893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88231","text":"Two rows are worth naming. "},{"id":"spn-88232","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SG9`"},{"id":"spn-88233","text":" holds the v0.4-2 rule "},{"id":"spn-88234","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"the seal judges legality\""},{"id":"spn-88235","text":": an illegal fan-out that lands two "},{"id":"spn-88236","marks":["code"],"text":"sig"},{"id":"spn-88237","text":" sources on one node expands "},{"id":"spn-88238","marks":["bold"],"text":"successfully"},{"id":"spn-88239","text":" — the prepass enforces only its own precondition — and is then rejected by the "},{"id":"spn-88240","marks":["bold"],"text":"seal"},{"id":"spn-88241","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-88242","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CONTROLLER_CONFLICT"},{"id":"spn-88243","text":". Sugar does not acquire a veto. "},{"id":"spn-88244","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SG12`"},{"id":"spn-88245","text":" proves the sugar-spelled world is genuinely "},{"id":"spn-88246","marks":["italic"],"text":"runnable"},{"id":"spn-88247","text":", folding "},{"id":"spn-88248","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 =="},{"id":"spn-88249","text":" the independent Fixture oracle; that is the row that would catch a desugar producing a well-formed-but-wrong graph, which "},{"id":"spn-88250","marks":["code"],"text":"SG2"},{"id":"spn-88251","text":" alone could not."}]},{"id":"blk-46894","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88252","text":"Three sub-decisions I made autonomously — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-46895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88253","text":"None can move an identity (they are all prepass-internal), but each is a "},{"id":"spn-88254","marks":["bold"],"text":"surface-language semantic"},{"id":"spn-88255","text":" that becomes expensive to change once authors write against it."}]},{"id":"blk-46896","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88256","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-a — group members are ZERO-BASED."},{"id":"spn-88257","text":" "},{"id":"spn-88258","marks":["code"],"text":"sp*3"},{"id":"spn-88259","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-88260","marks":["code"],"text":"sp0, sp1, sp2"},{"id":"spn-88261","text":". Rationale: matches the existing hand-written demo worlds ("},{"id":"spn-88262","marks":["code"],"text":"p0"},{"id":"spn-88263","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88264","marks":["code"],"text":"r0"},{"id":"spn-88265","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88266","marks":["code"],"text":"d0"},{"id":"spn-88267","text":", "},{"id":"spn-88268","marks":["code"],"text":"sp0"},{"id":"spn-88269","text":"). The alternative, one-based, reads better in prose but would contradict every world already in the tree."}]}],"id":"blk-46897","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88270","text":"**D-b — "},{"id":"spn-88271","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88272","text":" on both endpoints pairs POSITIONALLY, not cartesian.** "},{"id":"spn-88273","marks":["code"],"text":"[r*3] --sig--> [sp*3]"},{"id":"spn-88274","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-88275","marks":["bold"],"text":"3"},{"id":"spn-88276","text":" edges (i-th to i-th), not 9. Unequal counts are a typed rejection rather than a truncation or a broadcast. Rationale: the cartesian reading is almost always an error in this world model — "},{"id":"spn-88277","marks":["code"],"text":"sig"},{"id":"spn-88278","text":" fan-in is illegal anyway, so a 3×3 expansion would produce a graph the seal rejects six times over. Positional pairing is the only reading that is usually what was meant. "},{"id":"spn-88279","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88280","text":" on "},{"id":"spn-88281","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-88282","text":" endpoint still broadcasts to the whole group ("},{"id":"spn-88283","marks":["code"],"text":"SG5"},{"id":"spn-88284","text":"), which is the unambiguous case."}]}],"id":"blk-46899","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88285","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-c — an inline `;` comment on an expanded line attaches to the FIRST emitted line only."},{"id":"spn-88286","text":" The alternative — duplicating the comment onto all N — is noisier and would make the byte-exact no-op law harder to state. Line 0 keeps its original byte layout (and its comment) exactly; lines 1..N-1 are newly minted and carry no inherited alignment padding."}]}],"id":"blk-46901","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-46903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88287","text":"Happy to flip any of the three; "},{"id":"spn-88288","marks":["bold"],"text":"D-b"},{"id":"spn-88289","text":" is the one with real semantic weight."}]},{"id":"blk-46904","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88290","text":"7. The five questions"}]},{"id":"blk-46905","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46907","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88291","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q1 — Ratify the round-trip restatement?"},{"id":"spn-88292","text":" L1′ (world), L1″ (identity), L8′ (inverse run-input law) as stated in §2, with "},{"id":"spn-88293","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run6:83"},{"id":"spn-88294","text":" taking the same treatment. All three verified passing, none applied."}]}],"id":"blk-46906","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88295","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q2 — Which mouth is normative?"},{"id":"spn-88296","text":" §3 (a) status quo / (b) parser rejects / (c) parameterized, default strict."}]}],"id":"blk-46908","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88297","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q3 — Ratify the Core 0.1.2 errata?"},{"id":"spn-88298","text":" §4 — records shipped fact only; "},{"id":"spn-88299","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88300","text":" stays Reserved/partial."}]}],"id":"blk-46910","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46913","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88301","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q4 — Confirm or steer the Core 0.2 order?"},{"id":"spn-88302","text":" §5, and specifically whether L-1 "},{"id":"spn-88303","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-88304","text":" is the next language slice and whether the permission/instance split is the right frame for it."}]}],"id":"blk-46912","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-46915","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88305","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q5 — Confirm the three sugar sub-decisions?"},{"id":"spn-88306","text":" §6 D-a (zero-based), D-b (positional pairing), D-c (comment attachment). Shipped green; cheap to flip now, expensive later."}]}],"id":"blk-46914","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-46916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88307","text":"The Commit 8 open reversal ("},{"id":"spn-88308","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanV1"},{"id":"spn-88309","text":" carrying "},{"id":"spn-88310","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-88311","text":"s) is the networking track's question and is not restated here."}]},{"id":"blk-46917","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88312","text":"8. How to reproduce"}]},{"id":"blk-46918","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"cd TRVM/forge\nexport PYTHONPATH=../runtime/python:../research\n\n# the finding, measured -- ALL PASS\npython3 wrl_roundtrip_probe.py\n\n# the shipped sugar tier -- SG1-SG12 PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (~15s)\npython3 binding_run44.py\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run44.py  # ref-only\n\n# sugar regressions -- both green\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run11.py  # 3B-4  N1-N9\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run23.py  # v0.5-0 M1-M5 (~61s)\n\n# the three stale assertions, still red (unchanged by this memo)\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run9.py   # L1, L8 FAIL; L2-L7, L9, L10 PASS\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run6.py   # V1 OK, then AssertionError at :83\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run15.py  # S9 only -- unrelated root cause (~154s)"},{"id":"blk-46919","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-88313","text":"9. Files"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-46921","spans":[{"id":"spn-88314","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-46922","spans":[{"id":"spn-88315","text":"Change"}]}],"id":"blk-46920","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-46923","spans":[{"id":"spn-88316","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_roundtrip_probe.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46924","spans":[{"id":"spn-88317","marks":["bold"],"text":"new"},{"id":"spn-88318","text":" — measures the finding and executes the three proposed restatements. Not a battery; edits nothing."}]}],[{"id":"blk-46925","spans":[{"id":"spn-88319","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_sugar.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46926","spans":[{"id":"spn-88320","marks":["bold"],"text":"modified"},{"id":"spn-88321","text":" — adds the "},{"id":"spn-88322","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-88323","text":" replication and "},{"id":"spn-88324","marks":["code"],"text":"{...}"},{"id":"spn-88325","text":" fan-out prepass ahead of the existing value sugar. "},{"id":"spn-88326","marks":["code"],"text":"desugar_core"},{"id":"spn-88327","text":" becomes 1→many."}]}],[{"id":"blk-46927","spans":[{"id":"spn-88328","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run44.py"}]},{"id":"blk-46928","spans":[{"id":"spn-88329","marks":["bold"],"text":"new"},{"id":"spn-88330","text":" — SG1–SG12, the sugar-tier battery."}]}],[{"id":"blk-46929","spans":[{"id":"spn-88331","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_LANGUAGE_TRACK_MEMO.md"}]},{"id":"blk-46930","spans":[{"id":"spn-88332","marks":["bold"],"text":"new"},{"id":"spn-88333","text":" — this memo."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-46931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-88334","text":"One shipped module was modified ("},{"id":"spn-88335","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_sugar.py"},{"id":"spn-88336","text":"), additively and above the parser. "},{"id":"spn-88337","marks":["bold"],"text":"No identity moved"},{"id":"spn-88338","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-88339","marks":["code"],"text":"SG8"},{"id":"spn-88340","text":" proves it against the frozen demo id, and "},{"id":"spn-88341","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run11"},{"id":"spn-88342","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-88343","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run23"},{"id":"spn-88344","text":" prove the pre-existing value sugar is byte-unchanged. "},{"id":"spn-88345","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-88346","text":" was not promoted. No new runtime construct."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierafmpjlomckczziqr4jjtvjrfnhxqy4cn4kknkpevkuvissda6d6ha","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}